<programme channel="DocuBox.HD.fr" start="20261116070000 +0000" stop="20261116072500 +0000">
    <title lang="fr">Travel Thru History</title>
    <sub-title lang="fr">Savannah</sub-title>
    <desc lang="fr">We visit the old south and enjoy some sweet tea in Savannah. On this episode, we'll stroll the city's beautiful squares, as well as visit it's civil war past at Old Fort Jackson. Then, we head up the stairs of the famous Tybee Island lighthouse and visit the Savannah Railroad museum.</desc>
    <category lang="fr">Documentaire de société</category>
    <icon src="http://static-cdn.tv.sfr.net/data/img/pl/2/7/4/15270472.jpg" />
    <episode-num system="onscreen">E4</episode-num>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="DocuBox.HD.fr" start="20261116072500 +0000" stop="20261116075000 +0000">
    <title lang="fr">Travel Thru History</title>
    <sub-title lang="fr">St. Augustine</sub-title>
    <desc lang="fr">There's a lot to cover in the oldest city in America. Take a sip from the distinctively tasting Fountain of Youth. Then we'll cross the draw bridge of the undefeated Spanish Fort, the Castillo San Marcos. Then we'll learn the true history of pirates at the Pirate Museum.</desc>
    <category lang="fr">Documentaire de société</category>
    <icon src="http://static-cdn.tv.sfr.net/data/img/pl/2/7/4/15270472.jpg" />
    <episode-num system="onscreen">S1 E5</episode-num>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="DocuBox.HD.fr" start="20261116075000 +0000" stop="20261116082000 +0000">
    <title lang="fr">Nature's Force</title>
    <category lang="fr">Documentaire</category>
    <icon src="http://static-cdn.tv.sfr.net/data/img/pl/4/4/9/15271944.jpg" />
    <episode-num system="onscreen">S1 E6</episode-num>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="DocuBox.HD.fr" start="20261116082000 +0000" stop="20261116085000 +0000">
    <title lang="fr">Nature's Force</title>
    <desc lang="fr">Weather is universal and it's also Extra Terrestrial. Learn about space weather and how it can impact us on earth. Supercells are unique storms that scientists have learnt to measure into three types. Under the earth's crust, nature is extremely energetic, and we see this through the Volcano which acts as our eye into the forces beneath our feet. Learn about the purple buzzing glow called St Elmo's Fire, how it was named and were to look for it.</desc>
    <category lang="fr">Documentaire</category>
    <icon src="http://static-cdn.tv.sfr.net/data/img/pl/4/4/9/15271944.jpg" />
    <episode-num system="onscreen">S1 E7</episode-num>
  </programme>
  
